{
  "description": "Row batches in the journal payload of a one-phase branch (ClickHouse): versioned JSON, values JSON cannot carry exactly are tagged {\"$\": tag, \"v\": value} (uuid, decimal as text, bytes base64, date / datetime ISO 8601, float only when not finite, map for every object as [[key, value]]). a batch with \"erase\": true lists entities to erase (rows are their dat_id), and the flag is left out of insert batches. cases: payload decodes to batches (each value described as {type, value}: float as Python repr, bytes as hex, datetime as ISO 8601 with its offset or naive), and encoding those batches decodes back to the same values; byte-exact spelling is not required. errors: payloads every decoder rejects.",
